# Git and version control

## Before editing

1. `git status --short` and note current branch
2. Do not discard unrelated user changes
3. Prefer a feature branch (`cursor/<slug>-…`) over working directly on protected `main`
4. Warn if about to edit on a protected branch without an explicit brief

## Allowed (green — `agents/AUTONOMY.md`)

- Commit, push, open/update **draft** PRs for reversible Nortiqa work in this repo
- Small commits with clear messages
- Show modified files at session end

## Forbidden without explicit Gio authorization / red-zone handling

- `git push --force` / force-with-lease to shared branches unless Gio ordered recovery
- `git reset --hard` discarding foreign or unreviewed work
- Merge to `main` when policy requires human merge (default: leave draft PR ready)
- Destructive history rewriting

## Conflict note (agents)

Some task prompts say “no push”. In **this** repository, `agents/AUTONOMY.md` places draft PR push in the green zone for versionable work. Cloud/agent delivery follows AUTONOMY unless Gio issues a stricter session override.

## Commit messages

- Imperative, scoped: `feat(cursor): …`, `docs(dev): …`, `chore(agents): …`
- Explain why when non-obvious
